//! Cosines of the DCT basis, correctly rounded.
//!
//! GENERATED: `COS_PI_OVER_16[m]` is the nearest `f64` to the true cosine of the
//! `f64` value of `m * PI / 16`, computed to 80 significant digits. Do not edit
//! by hand.
//!
//! The tables exist because `f64::cos` is a platform libm call whose last bit is
//! not guaranteed: macOS and glibc disagree with each other, and both disagree
//! with the reference implementation's JavaScript engine, on a handful of these
//! arguments. One bit there is enough to flip a coefficient that quantises to
//! exactly half a step, so the same build on two machines would emit different
//! bitstreams. Reading the cosines out of a table removes that entirely.
//!
//! The index is `(2 * sample + 1) * frequency`, which reaches 105 for the 8-point
//! transform.

